<div class="wrap">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span><span>Refund policy</span>
  </nav>
</div>

<section class="wrap wrap-mid" style="padding-bottom:clamp(60px,8vw,110px)">
  <span class="eyebrow">Policy</span>
  <h1 style="margin:14px 0 18px">Refund &amp; returns policy</h1>
  <p class="lede">Thirty days, no restocking fee, and we pay the return postage when the fault is ours.</p>

  <div class="stack-32" style="margin-top:44px;font-size:0.94rem;line-height:1.9;color:var(--text-dim)">
    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">The short version</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <p>You have <strong class="gold">30 days from delivery</strong> to change your mind on anything unopened and
          unused. Tell us within that window and we will refund the full product cost. There is no restocking fee and
          no minimum order.</p>
        <p>If something arrived damaged, faulty, or is not what you ordered, the 30 days do not apply in the same way:
          tell us whenever you notice, and we will replace it or refund it. Faults are our problem, not yours.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">What can come back</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <p><strong class="gold">Tea, still sealed.</strong> Unopened tins, sealed pouches and untouched cakes in their
          original packaging can be returned. Tea is a food product, so once a seal is broken it cannot be resold and
          cannot be accepted back.</p>
        <p><strong class="gold">Tea you have opened and do not like.</strong> This is the case the rules do not cover
          well, so we simply do it anyway: tell us what is wrong with it and we will replace it or refund it. We do not
          ask you to ship a half-used tin back across a border. Please be reasonable about it and so will we — this is
          a standing offer, not a free refill.</p>
        <p><strong class="gold">Teaware.</strong> Returnable within 30 days, unused, in its packaging. A pot or a tray
          that has been used to brew with cannot be returned unless it is faulty.</p>
        <p><strong class="gold">Jade and jewellery.</strong> Returnable within 30 days in unworn condition, with the
          certificate or appraisal that came with it. A piece that has been worn, sized, engraved or altered is not
          returnable — it can no longer be sold as new, and for jade it can no longer be certified.</p>
        <p><strong class="gold">Gift sets and gift cards.</strong> Gift sets follow the rule for their contents. Gift
          cards are not refundable and cannot be exchanged for cash.</p>
        <p><strong class="gold">Made to order and personalised.</strong> Engraved, resized or bespoke pieces are made
          for you alone and cannot be returned unless they are faulty or not as specified. We say so on the product
          page before you buy, and we confirm the specification with you in writing first.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">How to return something</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <ol class="stack-8" style="padding-left:20px;list-style:decimal">
          <li>Email <a class="link-underline" href="mailto:<%= company.email %>"><%= company.email %></a> with your
            order number and what you would like to send back. A photograph helps enormously for anything damaged or
            faulty, and usually settles it without a return at all.</li>
          <li>We reply within <%= company.responseTime %> with return instructions and a return authorisation. Please
            do not post anything back before you have one — an unannounced parcel is hard to match to an order.</li>
          <li>Send the goods back within <strong class="gold">14 days</strong> of that authorisation, in the condition
            you received them, with any certificate or appraisal that came with them.</li>
          <li>We inspect the parcel when it arrives and email you to confirm, or to explain why it is not accepted.
            That is the point at which the refund is approved.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>For a damaged, faulty or wrong item we send a prepaid return label where the carrier offers one. For a
          change of mind, the return postage is yours.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">When the money comes back</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <p>Refunds are issued to the <strong class="gold">original card</strong> — we cannot refund to
          a different card, a different name, or as cash. We approve the refund within 2 business days of inspecting
          the return, and it normally appears on your statement within <strong class="gold">5 to 10 business
          days</strong> depending on your bank. Your bank controls that last part, not us.</p>
        <p>The refund covers the full product cost and any tax charged on it. Original shipping is refunded when the
          whole order is returned, or when the return is because of a fault or an error on our part. For a partial
          return of a change-of-mind order, the original shipping is not refunded.</p>
        <p>If an order is cancelled before it is dispatched we refund in full immediately. Once it is with the carrier
          it is a return, not a cancellation — but tell us quickly and we will often catch it before it leaves.</p>
        <p>Refused or undeliverable parcels that come back to us are refunded less the outbound shipping and any
          customs charges we were unable to recover.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">Orders that never arrive</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <p>Every parcel ships with tracking. If the tracking stops moving for 10 business days, or shows delivered
          when nothing arrived, tell us and we will open a claim with the carrier and either reship or refund — your
          choice, and we do not ask you to wait for the carrier's answer before we act.</p>
        <p>If a parcel is seized or destroyed by customs — which happens with unprocessed tea leaf in a few countries —
          we refund the product cost in full. Import duties and taxes are the customer's responsibility and cannot be
          refunded by us.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">Chargebacks and disputes</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <p>If a charge looks wrong, please contact us before calling your bank. A payment query is usually a
          misread date or a duplicated authorisation that has already been reversed, and we can show you the
          transaction record and fix it the same day. A chargeback takes weeks and costs us a fee whether or not we
          are right.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">Your statutory rights</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <p>Nothing in this policy replaces or limits the rights you have under the consumer law that applies where you
          live. Where a statutory right is stronger than what is written here — a longer cancellation window, or a
          remedy we have not listed — that right prevails, and you do not need to quote this page to use it.</p>
        <p class="tiny faint">Last updated <%= policy.updated %>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row" style="gap:12px;margin-top:40px;flex-wrap:wrap">
    <a class="btn btn-solid" href="/contact">Start a return</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/shipping">Shipping policy</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/terms">Terms of service</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/order">Track an order</a>
  </div>
</section>
